TYPES OF VARIABLE

	-- local variable (Stack) -- defined inside method, constructor or block
		** memory is allocated only when m/c/b are called
		** var in parameter is always a local variable
	-- instance variable (heap) -- defined inside class but outside the method/ constructor/block
		** memory is allocated when object is created
	-- static variable (non heap area) -- inside class outside M/C/B but with static variable.
		** when .class file is loaded(byte code)

	** return value is stored in stack


		instance var <- local var // directly
		this.inst var <- local var
		// but if the name are same the priority is given to local var and the value won't be assigned to the instance variable so for this we use this.var_name
		** this refer current class object


